  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models substantially outperform image-only models (best RNA ~0.653 vs best image ~0.227), scvi_n200 with multiprofile is the strongest RNA setup, and aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) has minimal impact for scvi. The critical open question is whether the weak image modality provides any complementary signal when fused with the strong RNA representation. This experiment (config_033) pairs our best RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) with resnet50 and weighted fusion, directly comparable to config_006 (0.653). Weighted fusion is chosen over concat because it can learn to downweight the much weaker image signal, giving the fairest test of whether image adds value. If this matches or beats 0.653, multimodal fusion is worth further exploration; if it falls short, we can confidently focus the remaining budget on RNA-only improvements (e.g., scgpt encoder) and skip the 30+ multimodal configurations. This single experiment resolves the highest-impact design decision under budget constraints."
}

